description: Never add Cursor Co-authored-by trailers to git commits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Git commit authorship

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor co-author trailer) to commits.
- Never ask the user to keep or restore that trailer.
- If the environment injects it automatically, strip it before the commit is finalized (e.g. via `prepare-commit-msg` hook) or amend/rewrite immediately when the user asks.
- Commit messages should attribute work only to the human author / repo conventions — no AI co-author footers.
